uest ception the objectives you  capture to take a sector can be thought  of as just  mini conquest within conquest what seems  to be different here are the vast spaces  between sectors so capturing one means  the enemy team gets pushed really far  away and you get time to regroup  breakthrough the second launch mode is  just having players fight in a single  sector  so really just cramming more players  into places they would already be in  conquest what's to be seen here is if  sectors properly divide up 128 players  as advertised  if we get too many players in one  location then you'll wind up just  spawning and dying instantly which can  become kind of tedious  to be fair some of you love 64 player op  metro and this might be your  jam so not everything got answered in  these presentations and we still have  some lingering questions  going through these in no particular  order how does vehicle play work when  everybody has a launcher and how will  vehicles hope to survive with that much  ordinance being shot at them  when launchers were tied to just the  engineer class at least there was a  limit to how many might be out there  will the new conquest work if it's  basically just conquest points within  conquest points  i know it's designed to spread players  out but what happens if players don't  ever fully capture sectors what happens  if an entire team just decides to roll  as a unit does this mean even more  people need to stick around to defend  objectives when players typically don't  like to do that something that will  probably be a dea play but  how is hazard zone not a battle royale  in this stream it was described as a  high-stakes squad-based mode that builds  tension as you play  which sounds super battle royale we do  know now that you can bring specialist  loadouts and gadgets with you so maybe  less scavenging is involved  but the hazard zone title definitely  sounds like areas of the map getting cut  off i mean call of duty black ops cold  war tri